This pattern is idiomatic when the index is needed (here i is used to index into anchors[validated.anchor_index] for the last cert). However, the loop can be more explicit about its intent by using enumerate with windows or a different structuring.

The concrete Clippy warning is not about this loop specifically — this is correct and readable. However, the check on the last element can be expressed more clearly:

  for (i, cert) in chain.iter().enumerate() {
      if i + 1 < chain.len() {
          revocation.check_revocation(cert, &chain[i + 1])?;
      } else {
          revocation.check_revocation_against_anchor(cert, &anchors[validated.anchor_index])?;
      }
  }

This removes the chain.get(i+1) unwrap and makes the two branches symmetric. Minor style improvement.
